Manage organisations — billing and a directory.

An organisation does not give anyone access to a vault. It owns a plan and a set of seats; a seat decides which plan's limits apply to the holder. Sharing a vault is `evnx vault share`, and only someone who holds the key can do it.

Usage: evnx org [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  create    Create an organisation. You become its owner
  list      List the organisations this account belongs to
  members   Who is in an organisation, and who holds a seat
  invite    Invite someone by email
  invites   Invitations sent but not yet redeemed
  uninvite  Withdraw an invitation
  accept    Redeem an invitation token
  billing   What this organisation is on, and until when
  seats     Show or set how many seats are purchased
  assign    Give someone a seat
  release   Take a seat back
  role      Change someone's role
  remove    Remove someone from an organisation
  delete    Delete an organisation
  leave     Leave an organisation
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --server <URL>
          evnx server to talk to. Overrides EVNX_SERVER and config.toml

      --no-color
          Disable colored output

  -q, --quiet
          Print nothing on success. Findings, warnings, errors and requested data still print

  -v, --verbose
          Enable verbose output

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Exit codes:
    0  Ran, nothing to report
    2  Could not run: usage, config, I/O, or refused before any change
    4  Declined: answered no, or a confirmation was needed with no terminal and no --yes
   10  Not signed in, or the token was rejected
   11  Forbidden, or the email is not verified
   12  The plan's limit is reached
   13  Server unreachable, not an evnx server, or TLS roots unusable
   14  Conflict, or locked
   15  Server error, or rate limited
  141  Output closed early (broken pipe)

Full guide: https://docs.evnx.dev/cli/commands/org
